════════════ ENGLISH ════════════

🔐 Password Manager

🎯 Objective

Build a local password manager protected by a master password, capable of storing, retrieving, generating, and deleting credentials — all encrypted at rest using a key derived from the master password.

⚙️ Features
✅ Master password setup and verification
✅ Password encryption using Fernet (AES)
✅ Key derivation from master password (PBKDF2)
✅ Automatic secure password generation
✅ Add, list, get, update, delete credentials
✅ Encrypted local storage in JSON format
✅ Sensitive data excluded from version control

---

🏗️ Project Structure
password-manager/
│
├── main.py          # Entry point & CLI routing
├── auth.py          # Master password hashing & verification
├── crypto.py        # Encryption, decryption, key derivation
├── generator.py     # Secure password generation
├── storage.py       # JSON load/save logic
├── passwords.json   # Encrypted credentials (gitignored)
├── master.hash      # Hashed master password (gitignored)
├── salt.bin         # Cryptographic salt (gitignored)
├── .gitignore
└── README.md

⚠️ master.hash, salt.bin, and passwords.json are excluded from version control via .gitignore.

---

▶️ Usage
First run — set up master password:

bash
python3 main.py <command>
# Prompts for master password creation on first use
Available commands:

bash
python3 main.py add --service github        # Add credentials
python3 main.py list                        # List all services
python3 main.py get --service github        # Get credentials
python3 main.py update --service github     # Update password
python3 main.py delete --service github     # Delete entry
Output example:

Master password: ••••••••
Access granted.
Username: aida
Password: mY$3cureP@ss

---

🔒 Security Overview
Mechanism	Description
bcrypt	Master password hashing
PBKDF2 + SHA-256	Key derivation (100 000 iterations)
os.urandom(16)	Random cryptographic salt
Fernet (AES-128)	Symmetric password encryption
getpass	Hidden password input
.gitignore	Secrets excluded from repo

---

🧠 Technical Concepts
Password hashing with bcrypt
Key derivation with PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256
Symmetric encryption/decryption with cryptography.fernet
Secure random generation with secrets
CLI argument parsing with argparse
File handling in binary and text modes
Modular architecture with separation of concerns
Defensive programming (missing files, wrong password, unknown service)

---

🚀 Design Choices
The encryption key is never stored — it is re-derived from the master password at each session.
bcrypt and PBKDF2 are used separately: one for authentication, one for encryption.
Sensitive files are excluded from Git from the start.
Modular structure makes each layer independently testable and extensible.

---

📌 Future Improvements
 Clipboard copy (auto-clear after 30s)
 Password strength indicator
 Export to encrypted CSV
 Unit tests with pytest
 Master password change support
 Search/filter by service name

 ---

📈 Level
Intermediate Python scripting project.
Focus on cryptographic security, modular architecture, and local secret management.


